WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.649 --> 00:00:03.229
- Here's my wonderful donkey, Thistle.

00:00:03.229 --> 00:00:05.088
Hello, you wanna come out?

00:00:05.088 --> 00:00:08.505
And she tells me, “Of course, am I stupid?”

00:00:09.784 --> 00:00:12.024
“Freedom,” she's saying, “Oh,

00:00:12.024 --> 00:00:14.948
it's a (beep)ing about
time you got here, yeah.”

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:18.082
There we are, a donkey that's weird.

00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:20.031
It was quite magical, talking to animals,

00:00:20.031 --> 00:00:22.303
'cause they're sharing
their experiences with you,

00:00:22.303 --> 00:00:25.253
they're giving you a
perspective into their world.

00:00:25.253 --> 00:00:27.423
Gonna go and see the others?

00:00:27.423 --> 00:00:28.752
Yep, okay.

00:00:28.752 --> 00:00:32.533
I do converse with my pets
on a day to day basis,

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:35.053
and we chat about the most unusual things.

00:00:35.053 --> 00:00:37.713
I've had the lectures
on American politics.

00:00:37.713 --> 00:00:39.046
You come closer?

00:00:39.992 --> 00:00:41.781
- [Camera Person] What's she saying?

00:00:41.781 --> 00:00:43.114
- Just, yum yum.

00:00:44.571 --> 00:00:46.553
Thistle's not sure how to behave now.

00:00:46.553 --> 00:00:49.514
He talks about crime shows, of all things.

00:00:49.514 --> 00:00:50.542
If we have the TV on,

00:00:50.542 --> 00:00:51.973
she'll be outside the door watching it.

00:00:51.973 --> 00:00:53.965
This is from her position, it's like,

00:00:53.965 --> 00:00:55.884
they've actually got a
really good storyline,

00:00:55.884 --> 00:00:57.493
but they've got to have strong characters,

00:00:57.493 --> 00:00:59.834
to actually bring it together.

00:00:59.834 --> 00:01:02.613
Probably the thing that
I learned as a child,

00:01:02.613 --> 00:01:04.973
is that you do get bombarded
with a lot of information

00:01:04.973 --> 00:01:06.851
from the animals.

00:01:06.851 --> 00:01:09.005
It just comes in all the time.

00:01:09.005 --> 00:01:11.714
You go outside, the
birds are talking to you.

00:01:11.714 --> 00:01:14.933
You sit on the grass, the
worms are talking to you.

00:01:14.933 --> 00:01:16.634
I'm getting a little
bit queasy here cause,

00:01:16.634 --> 00:01:20.032
I didn't realize, I'd actually
taken some spiderwebs down.

00:01:20.032 --> 00:01:22.794
I don't think he's lost
far, he's just in the house.

00:01:22.794 --> 00:01:25.293
Was going to have a Skype session
with my client in America,

00:01:25.293 --> 00:01:27.183
‘cause she's got a new kitten,

00:01:27.183 --> 00:01:29.683
but the kitten's gone missing.

00:01:30.613 --> 00:01:31.983
Hi.

00:01:31.983 --> 00:01:33.554
- [Client] I can't find him.

00:01:33.554 --> 00:01:36.143
- Tell me where you've looked.

00:01:36.143 --> 00:01:37.594
- [Client] All over our house.

00:01:37.594 --> 00:01:38.834
- I would just keep talking to him,

00:01:38.834 --> 00:01:41.453
and see if we can get him to
come out, and show himself.

00:01:41.453 --> 00:01:43.506
- [Client] Will he come to Finn?

00:01:43.506 --> 00:01:45.085
- [Faye] He will.

00:01:45.085 --> 00:01:49.215
- [Client] Finn, kitty,
kitty, kitty, kitty, Finn?

00:01:49.215 --> 00:01:51.298
Can he hear us right now?

00:01:52.535 --> 00:01:53.368
- No.

00:01:54.557 --> 00:01:56.285
To communicate with any animal,

00:01:56.285 --> 00:01:58.765
they don't have to be present with me,

00:01:58.765 --> 00:02:00.117
so what I'm trying to do is just

00:02:00.117 --> 00:02:02.542
to get Finn to share about his day.

00:02:02.542 --> 00:02:06.702
This is just random impressions
that have come through.

00:02:06.702 --> 00:02:07.869
It is my game.

00:02:10.555 --> 00:02:11.888
I will be found.

00:02:16.014 --> 00:02:17.174
When you're a child,

00:02:17.174 --> 00:02:19.334
the power of the
imagination is so powerful.

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:23.042
I mean, what is reality
and what's not reality?

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:25.321
I remember a few
childhood experiences with

00:02:25.321 --> 00:02:28.374
animals would be telling me
things and I would tell my mum,

00:02:28.374 --> 00:02:32.541
and she would say, "Animals
don't talk, it's cartoons."

00:02:33.955 --> 00:02:35.245
Hello!

00:02:35.245 --> 00:02:37.743
- [Client] Hi, I found Finn.

00:02:37.743 --> 00:02:39.010
Isn't he gorgeous?

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.892
- He's actually just so relieved.

00:02:40.892 --> 00:02:43.642
He's enjoyed all the dramatics over him.

00:02:43.642 --> 00:02:45.804
- You're wonderful with what you do.

00:02:45.804 --> 00:02:48.412
I feel more connected with the animals,

00:02:48.412 --> 00:02:51.572
it brings joy and also
brings a little sorrow,

00:02:51.572 --> 00:02:52.703
and a little pain.

00:02:52.703 --> 00:02:56.870
But, I don't know what I would
do, if I didn't have you.

